Project Development

ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models

1. Project Development Overview

ComicCraft is developed as an AI-based web application that converts a user's simple story idea into a structured comic story. The application uses Google Gemini models to generate the story, characters, dialogues, scenes, and panel descriptions.

The development is divided into several modules to make the system easy to build, test, and maintain.


---

2. Development Modules

Module 1 – User Interface

The frontend provides an easy-to-use interface where users can:

Enter a comic/story idea.

Select genre and story style.

Enter character details.

Select the number of comic panels.

Generate and edit the comic.

Preview the final result.


Technologies: HTML, CSS, JavaScript / React.


---

Module 2 – User Authentication

This module manages:

User registration.

Login and logout.

User profile.

Secure authentication.


User-specific comic projects can be stored and accessed through their account.


---

Module 3 – AI Story Generation

This is the core module of ComicCraft.

The user's prompt is sent to the Gemini API. Gemini processes the prompt and generates:

Story title

Story plot

Characters

Character personalities

Scenes

Dialogues

Narration


Example:

Input:

> "Create a superhero comic about a college student who discovers a mysterious power."



AI Output:
A structured superhero story with characters, scenes, dialogues, and panel descriptions.


---

Module 4 – Comic Panel Generation

The generated story is divided into multiple panels.

Each panel contains:

Component	Description

Panel Number	Position of the panel
Scene	Description of the location/action
Characters	Characters appearing in the scene
Dialogue	Character conversation
Narration	Story narration
Visual Prompt	Description for creating the comic artwork



---

Module 5 – Comic Editor

Users can modify the AI-generated content.

Features include:

Edit story text.

Change character names.

Modify dialogues.

Edit scenes.

Regenerate individual panels.

Change panel order.


This allows users to maintain creative control over AI-generated content.


---

Module 6 – Comic Preview

The completed comic is displayed in a comic-book-style layout.

The preview includes:

Comic panels

Character dialogues

Speech bubbles

Captions

Scene descriptions/images where supported


Users can review the comic before exporting it.


---

Module 7 – Database Management

The database stores:

User information

Comic projects

Story content

Character information

Panel details

Generated prompts


Possible database technologies include MySQL, MongoDB, or Firebase.


---

Module 8 – Export Module

After completing the comic, users can export it.

Possible formats:

PDF

PNG/JPG images

Digital comic format


The exported file maintains the panel sequence and generated content.


---

3. Gemini API Integration

The application communicates with Gemini through an API request.

Basic process:

User Prompt
     ↓
ComicCraft Frontend
     ↓
Backend Server
     ↓
Gemini API
     ↓
AI Generated Story
     ↓
Comic Panel Structure
     ↓
Comic Preview

A structured prompt is sent to Gemini so that the response can be easily converted into comic panels.


