6. Testing During Development

The following testing methods are used:

Unit Testing: Tests individual modules.

Integration Testing: Tests communication between frontend, backend, database, and Gemini API.

Functional Testing: Ensures all features work according to requirements.

UI Testing: Checks interface and navigation.

API Testing: Verifies Gemini API requests and responses.

User Acceptance Testing: Ensures the application meets user expectations.



